        content: `# Day 5: Build Your Portfolio (Fast) 🎨\n\n## No Clients? No Problem.\n\nYou don't need real clients to have a real portfolio. Here's how to build one today.\n\n## The Spec Work Strategy\n\nCreate samples for **imaginary or real brands** that showcase your skills.\n\n### Method 1: Pick Real Brands\nChoose 3 businesses in your target market and create sample work:\n\n\`\`\`\nI want to create a portfolio sample for my [gig type] service.\nCreate a [deliverable] for [a real local business type] as if \nthey were my client. Make it impressive and realistic.\n\nBusiness: [describe a realistic business]\nTheir need: [what they'd want from your service]\nDeliverable: [what you'd create for them]\n\`\`\`\n\n### Method 2: Case Study Format\nMore powerful than just showing the work:\n\n1. **The Problem** — What the client needed\n2. **The Approach** — How you used AI + your skills\n3. **The Result** — What you delivered\n4. **The Impact** — Projected results (e.g., "This strategy could increase engagement by 40%")\n\n## Where to Host Your Portfolio\n\n- **Notion** — Free, professional-looking pages\n- **Carrd** — $19/year for a slick one-pager\n- **Google Drive** — Simple but effective for docs\n- **Behance/Dribbble** — For design work\n- **Medium** — For writing samples\n\n## Quick Portfolio Template\n\n\`\`\`\nCreate a portfolio page layout for my [gig] service.\nInclude:\n- Headline that hooks potential clients\n- 3 sample project descriptions with results\n- My process (how I work)\n- A clear call to action\n\`\`\`\n\n> 🎨 **Quality > Quantity**: 3 excellent samples beat 10 mediocre ones.`
