        content: `# Day 6: Set Up Your Business Basics 🏢\n\n## Look Professional from Day 1\n\nFirst impressions matter. Even as a side gig, looking professional builds trust.\n\n## Essential Setup Checklist\n\n### 1. Professional Email\n- Use: yourname@yourdomain.com or yourname.gig@gmail.com\n- Avoid: cooldude99@hotmail.com 😅\n\n### 2. LinkedIn Optimization\n\`\`\`\nHelp me update my LinkedIn profile to attract clients \nfor my [gig type] side business.\n\nCurrent role: [your job]\nSide gig: [your service]\nTarget clients: [who you serve]\n\nWrite:\n- A headline that mentions my service\n- A 3-paragraph "About" section\n- A featured section description\n\`\`\`\n\n### 3. Elevator Pitch\n\`\`\`\nCreate a 30-second elevator pitch for my side gig.\nI help [who] do [what] using [how/AI tools].\nThe result is [benefit].\nMake it conversational and memorable.\n\`\`\`\n\n### 4. Simple Contract Template\n\`\`\`\nCreate a simple freelance service agreement for my \n[gig type] business. Include:\n- Scope of work\n- Payment terms\n- Revision policy\n- Timeline\n- Cancellation policy\nKeep it professional but not overly legal.\n\`\`\`\n\n## Payment Setup\n- **Stripe** — Professional invoicing\n- **PayPal** — Universal acceptance\n- **Wise** — Great for international clients\n\n> 🏢 **You're not just freelancing. You're running a micro-business.** Treat it that way from the start.`
